	/vms/ gwacx /vm /			# btrfs subvolume sor vm #2

- vmware is basing its NFS files locks on the nfs fileid field returned fro=
m a NFS GETATTR request for the file being locked
	http://kb.vmware.com/selfservice/microsites/search.do?language=3Den_US&cmd=
=3DdisplayKC&externalId=3D1007909
   vmware assumes that these nfs fileid are unique per storage.

- it seemed that these nfs fileid are only unique 'per-subvolume', but beca=
use my nfs export contains many subvolumes,
the nfs export has then my files (in different subvolume) with the same nfs=
 fileid.

- no problem when I start all machine alone, but when 2 machines are runnin=
g at the same time, vmware seems to mix its reference to lock file and=20
sometimes kills one vm.

	in esx server, following messages : 	/var/log/vmkwarning.log :=20

